From: X1407QA hardware recovery <local@x1407qa.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] pwrseq: qcom: diagnose WCN6855 stabilization delay

The native WCN6855 sequence waits 50 ms after target enablement. The
historical X1407QA recovery path held the WCN rails for about 6000 ms
before PCI enumeration and reached MHI Mission mode.

Change only the WCN6855 power-up delay to 6000 ms and emit a diagnostic
marker when that delay is used. Leave GPIO timing, PCI ordering, ath11k,
DT and USB untouched.

This is a machine-specific diagnostic patch, not a proposed upstream fix.
---
 drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
index d41793e1fcd9..f8c2c579988a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
+++ b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
@@ -235,8 +235,11 @@ static int pwrseq_qcom_wcn_pwup_delay(struct pwrseq_device *pwrseq)
 {
 	struct pwrseq_qcom_wcn_ctx *ctx = pwrseq_device_get_drvdata(pwrseq);
 
-	if (ctx->pdata->pwup_delay_ms)
+	if (ctx->pdata->pwup_delay_ms) {
+		if (ctx->pdata->pwup_delay_ms == 6000)
+			pr_info("X1407QA Wi-Fi diagnostic: WCN6855 stabilization delay 6000 ms\n");
 		msleep(ctx->pdata->pwup_delay_ms);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -379,6 +382,6 @@ static const struct pwrseq_qcom_wcn_pdata pwrseq_wcn6855_of_data = {
 	.vregs = pwrseq_wcn6855_vregs,
 	.num_vregs = ARRAY_SIZE(pwrseq_wcn6855_vregs),
-	.pwup_delay_ms = 50,
+	.pwup_delay_ms = 6000,
 	.gpio_enable_delay_ms = 5,
 	.targets = pwrseq_qcom_wcn6855_targets,
 };
-- 
